# Convert Tab-Based Navigation to React Router with Separate Page Directories

## Background

Currently, the app uses a single `App.tsx` with a `useState`-based `activeTab` pattern to switch between 8 views (home, challenges, submit-challenge, ai-triage, university, industry, lifecycle, analytics, communication). All views are conditionally rendered in a single component, with shared state (problems, analytics, proposals, etc.) living in `App.tsx`.

This plan converts the app to use **React Router** with proper URL-based routing and a dedicated `pages/` directory for each page, while preserving all existing functionality.

## Proposed Changes

### Install React Router

#### [NEW] `react-router-dom` dependency
- Run `npm install react-router-dom` to add client-side routing.

---

### New `pages/` Directory

Each page will be a thin wrapper component that receives shared data/handlers from the layout and renders the existing component. The existing components in `components/` remain **untouched** — no changes to their props or internal logic.

#### [NEW] `src/pages/HomePage.tsx`
- Extracts the current `HomeView` function from `App.tsx` into its own page file.
- Route: `/`

#### [NEW] `src/pages/ChallengesPage.tsx`
- Wraps `<CitizenModule />` with the props it needs from the layout context.
- Route: `/challenges`

#### [NEW] `src/pages/SubmitChallengePage.tsx`
- Wraps `<CitizenSubmissionView />`.
- Route: `/submit-challenge`

#### [NEW] `src/pages/AITriagePage.tsx`
- Wraps `<AIProblemManagement />`.
- Route: `/ai-triage`

#### [NEW] `src/pages/UniversityPage.tsx`
- Wraps `<UniversityModule />`.
- Route: `/university`

#### [NEW] `src/pages/IndustryPage.tsx`
- Wraps `<IndustryModule />`.
- Route: `/industry`

#### [NEW] `src/pages/LifecyclePage.tsx`
- Wraps `<ProjectLifecycleView />`.
- Route: `/lifecycle`

#### [NEW] `src/pages/AnalyticsPage.tsx`
- Wraps `<AnalyticsDashboard />`.
- Route: `/analytics`

#### [NEW] `src/pages/CommunicationPage.tsx`
- Wraps `<CommunicationHub />`.
- Route: `/communication`

---

### Shared State: AppContext

#### [NEW] `src/AppContext.tsx`
- A React Context + Provider that holds all the shared state and handler functions currently in `App.tsx`:
  - `problems`, `analytics`, `universities`, `industryPartners`, `proposals`, `notifications`
  - `userRole`, `setUserRole`
  - `selectedProblem`, `setSelectedProblem`
  - `mapFilter`, `setMapFilter`, `trackingFilterCode`, `setTrackingFilterCode`
  - All handler functions: `handleUpvote`, `handleAssignHEI`, `handleSubmitProposal`, `handlePledgeFunding`, `handleUpdateMilestone`, `handleMarkNotificationRead`, `handleMarkAllNotificationsRead`, `handleSearchTrackingCode`
  - `isLoading`, `loadAllData`
- A `useAppContext()` hook for easy consumption in page components.

---

### Layout Component

#### [NEW] `src/components/Layout.tsx`
- Contains the persistent UI shell shared across all pages:
  - Language toggle (top-left)
  - Notification bell trigger (top-right)
  - Chat/Forum FAB (bottom-right)
  - `<NotificationPanel />`
  - `<ProblemDetailsModal />`
  - Footer
  - Loading spinner (when `isLoading`)
- Uses `<Outlet />` from React Router to render the active page.
- The "Back to Home" button on sub-pages is replaced by React Router's `<Link to="/">` (rendered inside each page or a shared sub-header within the Layout).

---

### Core File Changes

#### [MODIFY] `src/main.tsx`
- Wrap the app with `<BrowserRouter>` and `<AppProvider>`.
- Structure: `LanguageProvider > BrowserRouter > AppProvider > App`

#### [MODIFY] `src/App.tsx`
- **Dramatically simplified**: removes all state, handlers, and conditional rendering.
- Becomes a pure routing shell that defines `<Routes>` with the `<Layout>` as the parent route and each page as a child route.
- All `setActiveTab(...)` calls throughout the codebase will be replaced with `useNavigate()` calls.

---

### Component Navigation Updates

The home page cards currently call `setActiveTab('challenges')` etc. These will be updated to use React Router's `useNavigate()`:

#### [MODIFY] `src/components/CitizenModule.tsx`
- The `onOpenSubmitModal` prop currently calls `setActiveTab('submit-challenge')` — this comes from the parent, so no change needed inside CitizenModule itself. The parent (page wrapper) will pass `() => navigate('/submit-challenge')`.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> All existing component files in `src/components/` will have **zero internal changes**. Their callback props are already abstract (e.g., `onOpenSubmitModal: () => void`). The page wrappers will simply wire these callbacks to `navigate()` calls instead of `setActiveTab()` calls.

---

### Server-Side SPA Fallback

#### [MODIFY] `server.ts`
- Add a catch-all route that serves `index.html` for any non-API, non-static route, so direct URL access and browser refresh work correctly on all routes.

